\title{dbSNP4Bioc: build, cache, and query dbSNP VCF data as Parquet}
\description{
Converts a single chromosome of an NCBI dbSNP VCF (as distributed,
bgzipped and tabix-indexed) into a slim, sorted Parquet representation
with \code{\link[=dbsnp_build_chrom]{dbsnp_build_chrom()}}, caches it with
\code{\link[BiocFileCache:BiocFileCache]{BiocFileCache::BiocFileCache()}}, and exposes the cached resource as a
lazy \code{dplyr}/\code{dbplyr} table with \code{\link[=dbsnp_tbl]{dbsnp_tbl()}} so that rsID and
genomic-position lookups can be expressed with ordinary
\code{dplyr::filter()} / \code{dplyr::select()} pipelines.
}
\section{Workflow}{

\enumerate{
\item Set the environment variable \code{DBSNP_GCF_PATH} to the bgzipped,
tabix-indexed dbSNP VCF (e.g. \code{GCF_000001405.40.gz}, with
\code{GCF_000001405.40.gz.tbi} next to it).
\item Call \code{\link[=dbsnp_build_chrom]{dbsnp_build_chrom()}} once per chromosome of interest; this
populates the local BiocFileCache.
\item Call \code{\link[=dbsnp_tbl]{dbsnp_tbl()}} (or the convenience wrapper
\code{\link[=dbsnp_in_range]{dbsnp_in_range()}}) to query the cache with \code{dplyr} verbs.
}
